==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gd}} {{term|tàrmachan}}. The ''pt-'' comes from a mistaken Greek construction.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈtɑːmɪɡən/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|pl2=ptarmigan|s}}

# Any of three [[species]] of small [[grouse]] in the [[genus]] [[Lagopus]] found in [[subarctic]] [[tundra]] areas of [[North America]] and [[Eurasia]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|species of small grouse}} {{l|en|lagopus}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}

====Derived terms====
* Rock Ptarmigan
* White-tailed Ptarmigan
* Willow Ptarmigan

